invariant: INV-16
file: p256_field.c
catches: p256_field_test
reason: dropping the complement inverts the conditional subtraction: the
  value is reduced exactly when it is already below p and left alone when
  it is not, so every sum and every Montgomery product leaves the field.
  The mask is the one thing in this file that a reader cannot check by
  eye, and it is what constant time costs here, so the vectors have to
  fail on it.

--- old
    select_limbs(o, reduced, t, ~(uint32_t)(below >> 32));
--- new
    select_limbs(o, reduced, t, (uint32_t)(below >> 32));
